# libzhuyin.alloc — the allocator-pairing register for the zhuyin C ABI.
#
# Sibling of `libzhuyin.ver` and of `crates/oxpinyin-capi/libpinyin.alloc`,
# which carries the full format description and the rationale for each
# class. `tools/abi/check-alloc-pairing.sh` reads both registers the same
# way: it proves the register covers exactly the pointer-shaped slots
# `zhuyin.h` declares, that each class agrees with the C type, and — by
# running a C++ consumer under LeakSanitizer — that the declared
# deallocator is the one that actually releases the allocation.
#
# Format: <symbol>  <slot>  <class>  <notes>; `#` comments, blanks ignored.
# Classes: handle:<fn> | g_free | g_strfreev | borrowed.
# Notes: false-allocates | false-nulls | false-untouched | false-unreachable
# | n/a — each EXECUTABLE, probed by alloc-pairing-zhuyin.cc against a
# failure path a conforming consumer can reach.
#
# The zhuyin facade allocates through its own `ffi.rs` — `owned_cstr` and
# `owned_cstr_list` are duplicated from the pinyin one by design, because
# each is itself the unsafe edge and the constitution's unsafe allowlist
# reaches only the two C-ABI crates. (The doc-light boilerplate above the
# allocator — the handle casts and the `char **`-out sentence writer — is
# macro-stamped from `oxpinyin-capi-marshal` since 2026-09-10; the
# allocator boundary these registers describe is not.) The two registers
# are therefore checked separately rather than shared.

# ── Handles: allocated by Box::into_raw, released by their destructor ──
zhuyin_init                              return      handle:zhuyin_fini            n/a
zhuyin_alloc_instance                    return      handle:zhuyin_free_instance   n/a
zhuyin_begin_add_phrases                 return      handle:zhuyin_end_add_phrases n/a

# ── Borrowed pointers: never freed by the caller ──────────────────────
# The key getters NULL their out-param on the reachable refusal (no key at
# the offset); the string getters' only non-NULL-argument `false` needs an
# unset ChewingKey, which an opaque typedef denies a conforming consumer.
zhuyin_get_candidate                     candidate   borrowed                      false-nulls
zhuyin_get_candidate_string              utf8_str    borrowed                      false-unreachable
zhuyin_get_zhuyin_key                    key         borrowed                      false-nulls
zhuyin_get_zhuyin_key_rest               key_rest    borrowed                      false-nulls

# ── Caller-owned strings (g_free) ─────────────────────────────────────
zhuyin_get_sentence                      sentence    g_free                        false-nulls
zhuyin_get_zhuyin_string                 utf8_str    g_free                        false-unreachable
zhuyin_get_pinyin_string                 utf8_str    g_free                        false-unreachable
zhuyin_token_get_phrase                  utf8_str    g_free                        false-nulls

# ── Caller-owned string vectors (g_strfreev) ──────────────────────────
zhuyin_in_chewing_keyboard               symbols     g_strfreev                    false-nulls
